  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase IV of Supporting the Productive Integration of Venezuelan Refugees and Migrants in Latin America Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project proposal is for the fourth phase of the EiM program, and seeks to raise the visibility of challenges faced by migrant and host communities in the LATAM region and how innovative approaches to socio-economic integration leads to better outcomes, more resilience and a more empowered community for all. This fourth phase will be implemented through a communication strategy that involves the development and dissemination of captivating multimedia products and participation in strategic visibility events with key stakeholders in Ecuador, Peru and the United States. By raising awareness and visibility of the challenges faced by migrants and host communities and how programs like EiM help communities overcome these issues with key stakeholders and potential future funders, IOM aims to continue aiding the socio-economic integration of displaced people, highlighting the program&#x2019;s capacity to scale and replicate as well as demonstrating its success in bringing economic resilience to the region.</narrative>
  </description>
